["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"Yao Song: physical AI is won by systems, not by young geniuses From DeePhi to Orienspace to Striding AI, Yao Song (姚颂) argues that what decides physical AI is not one or two genius algorithms but data, compute, a talent pool and commercial delivery at every milestone — and that the intelligence-first giants may not be the ones who get to pick the fruit. 晚点聊 LateTalk 晚点聊 173: 对话姚颂：深鉴、东方空间、再出发，「天才少年」十年后 Physical AI Embodied intelligence Commercial spaceflight Startup playbook Tsinghua network AI chips WAM (world action model) VLA (vision-language-action model) latent space egocentric data teleoperation\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-21-latetalk-姚颂十年三次创业-物理ai的答案不是小天才-而是系统/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/e4332dff9f12ac9e-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"晚\"><span class=\"dur\">2:55:18</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">晚点聊 LateTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0721</span></div>\n<h2>Yao Song: physical AI is won by systems, not by young geniuses</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">From DeePhi to Orienspace to Striding AI, Yao Song (<span lang=\"zh\">姚颂</span>) argues that what decides physical AI is not one or two genius algorithms but data, compute, a talent pool and commercial delivery at every milestone — and that the intelligence-first giants may not be the ones who get to pick the fruit.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Physical AI</span><span class=\"tag\">Embodied intelligence</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Open weights now trail closed models by 3-5 months, and that lag is the whole safety margin Kimi K3 compresses the open-versus-closed gap from the 6-9 months people had been arguing over down to 3-5 months, and that lag is the only risk buffer anyone has — heavy-handed regulation of open weights would merely postpone the inevitable while voiding the buffer itself. Interconnects Interconnects Kimi K3: The open-weights escalation Open weights US-China competition Capital efficiency MoE architecture AI policy Kimi Delta Attention (KDA) Attention Residuals (AttnRes) Stable LatentMoE adversarial distillation decelerationist Entity List\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-20-interconnects-开闭源差距只剩-3-5-个月-这层时间差就是全部的安全边际/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/4ffff5b76a790c6c-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">20:03</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Interconnects</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0720</span></div>\n<h2>Open weights now trail closed models by 3-5 months, and that lag is the whole safety margin</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Kimi K3 compresses the open-versus-closed gap from the 6-9 months people had been arguing over down to 3-5 months, and that lag is the only risk buffer anyone has — heavy-handed regulation of open weights would merely postpone the inevitable while voiding the buffer itself.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Open weights</span><span class=\"tag\">US-China competition</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Why cross-entropy loss won: it is training a text compressor Cross-entropy loss was selected because it can be proved mathematically to be the only functional form that guarantees the loss is minimized exactly when the model&#x27;s output equals the true distribution of the data — and that turns out to be equivalent to training the model into a text compressor approaching the Shannon limit. Andrej Karpathy Andrej Karpathy But what is cross-entropy? | Compression is Intelligence Part 2 Information theory Cross-entropy Language model training Distillation Compression KL divergence cross-entropy KL divergence (relative entropy) distillation Lagrange multiplier Shannon limit\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-16-karpathy-训练语言模型本质上是在训练一个文本压缩器/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/ca853744f8d1a48a-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"A\"></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Andrej Karpathy</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0716</span></div>\n<h2>Why cross-entropy loss won: it is training a text compressor</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Cross-entropy loss was selected because it can be proved mathematically to be the only functional form that guarantees the loss is minimized exactly when the model&#x27;s output equals the true distribution of the data — and that turns out to be equivalent to training the model into a text compressor approaching the Shannon limit.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Information theory</span><span class=\"tag\">Cross-entropy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"The naked mole-rat queen rules with a $5 molecule: not urine, a skincare ingredient The signal that suppresses reproduction in naked mole-rats has finally been found: only the queen produces isopropyl myristate. Add it to a colony that has lost its queen and the peace holds; stop, and the succession war breaks out. The same molecule turns up on breastfeeding women. Nature Podcast Nature Podcast ‘Holy grail’ of naked mole-rat research reveals how queens rule naked mole-rats chemical signalling behavioural ecology cognitive science AI reasoning exoplanets isopropyl myristate naked mole-rat super-puff intuitive gamer\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-15-naturepod-裸鼹鼠女王不靠尿液-靠一种5美元分子维持王位/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/9b247947db171866-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"N\"><span class=\"dur\">22:40</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Nature Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0715</span></div>\n<h2>The naked mole-rat queen rules with a $5 molecule: not urine, a skincare ingredient</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The signal that suppresses reproduction in naked mole-rats has finally been found: only the queen produces isopropyl myristate. Add it to a colony that has lost its queen and the peace holds; stop, and the succession war breaks out. The same molecule turns up on breastfeeding women.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">naked mole-rats</span><span class=\"tag\">chemical signalling</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"Two or three assisted-driving suppliers will be left, and the window shuts by year-end Momenta&#x27;s Cao Xudong (曹旭东) argues that assisted driving is like batteries — there is only good and better — so the endgame leaves two or three third-party suppliers in China and three or four globally; the first tier already holds 90% market share, a data flywheel plus mass production is the ticket in, and the next stop is physical AI and home robots. 晚点聊 LateTalk 晚点聊 172: Momenta IPO后再访曹旭东：就是想做没有尽头的AI Assisted driving Robotics Data flywheel Physical AI Momenta Startup management world model RoboVan RoboTruck post-train data scaling\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-15-latetalk-智驾好和更好的行业-只容得下两三家/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/8cd6cf382873d1be-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"晚\"><span class=\"dur\">2:03:20</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">晚点聊 LateTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0715</span></div>\n<h2>Two or three assisted-driving suppliers will be left, and the window shuts by year-end</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Momenta&#x27;s Cao Xudong (<span lang=\"zh\">曹旭东</span>) argues that assisted driving is like batteries — there is only good and better — so the endgame leaves two or three third-party suppliers in China and three or four globally; the first tier already holds 90% market share, a data flywheel plus mass production is the ticket in, and the next stop is physical AI and home robots.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>2</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Assisted driving</span><span class=\"tag\">Robotics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"A black hole is a 100%-efficient power plant; fusion only reaches one percent Winch a brick slowly down to just above the horizon and let go, and 100% of its rest energy can become work far away; chemical burning gets one part in ten billion and fusion one percent, because nuclear reactions never touch the rest mass of protons and neutrons — only gravity does. Dwarkesh Podcast Dwarkesh Adam Brown – A deep but accessible introduction to general relativity General relativity Black holes Energy efficiency AI for science String theory History of physics equivalence principle fictitious / inertial force Schwarzschild radius / event horizon gravitational time dilation spaghettification\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-10-dwarkesh-黑洞是效率-100-的发电厂-聚变只到百分之一/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/9cb4dda1cfbcd52e-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"D\"><span class=\"dur\">1:38:24</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Dwarkesh Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0710</span></div>\n<h2>A black hole is a 100%-efficient power plant; fusion only reaches one percent</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Winch a brick slowly down to just above the horizon and let go, and 100% of its rest energy can become work far away; chemical burning gets one part in ten billion and fusion one percent, because nuclear reactions never touch the rest mass of protons and neutrons — only gravity does.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">General relativity</span><span class=\"tag\">Black holes</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"American Money Controls 11 Premier League Clubs, and Football Is Not the Point US capital now controls 11 Premier League clubs, and it has reached into UEFA commercial rights, broadcast distribution and the financing of player transfers; with media-rights income at its ceiling, it keeps playing by pushing valuations up and rolling assets through evergreen funds. 硅谷101 硅谷101 E243｜特朗普“缓刑”红牌之外，美国资本如何硬控全球足坛 Sports Investing Premier League US Capital Football Business Leveraged Buyouts Leveraged Buyout Asset Securitization Evergreen Fund Super League Matchday Revenue\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-10-sv101-美国资本硬控足坛-不只买队-还在收租/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/cfe8fa9f8e3fa476-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"硅\"><span class=\"dur\">1:16:28</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">硅谷101</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0710</span></div>\n<h2>American Money Controls 11 Premier League Clubs, and Football Is Not the Point</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">US capital now controls 11 Premier League clubs, and it has reached into UEFA commercial rights, broadcast distribution and the financing of player transfers; with media-rights income at its ceiling, it keeps playing by pushing valuations up and rolling assets through evergreen funds.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Sports Investing</span><span class=\"tag\">Premier League</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"Two ways to live in short drama: scale protects the capital, content runs on relationships Short drama has two survival modes: the scale mode runs on capital safety and the near-certain returns of 300 titles a month, the content mode on character relationships that determine motive; both sides think AI cannot replace a live actor&#x27;s micro-expressions for now. 乱翻书 乱翻书 269. 卷规模 VS 卷创作：真人短剧的两种生存模式 Live-action shorts Capacity management Content method AI disruption Female-audience hits Interactive film games RY (input-to-output ratio, return multiple) DIT (Digital Imaging Technician) Zhanshaxian (斩杀线), the kill line Jinshouzhi (金手指), the protagonist&#x27;s cheat power\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-09-luanfanshu-月产-300-部短剧不靠灵感-靠本金安全与人物关系/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/1b655f3a7a4cc727-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"乱\"><span class=\"dur\">1:11:37</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">乱翻书</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0709</span></div>\n<h2>Two ways to live in short drama: scale protects the capital, content runs on relationships</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Short drama has two survival modes: the scale mode runs on capital safety and the near-certain returns of 300 titles a month, the content mode on character relationships that determine motive; both sides think AI cannot replace a live actor&#x27;s micro-expressions for now.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Live-action shorts</span><span class=\"tag\">Capacity management</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"Self-evolving AI could close the loop in six months, but the model will quietly drift The inflection point for RSI is models becoming capable of long-horizon tasks. Apodex&#x27;s chief scientist says the self-evolution loop could close in as little as six months, but recursive drift and the model&#x27;s taste will need human gatekeeping for a long time yet. 硅谷101 硅谷101 E242｜最快半年AI跑通自进化？与陈天桥首席科学家聊聊硅谷模型必争之地 AI self-evolution RSI Long-horizon tasks Agent teams Model taste Research automation RSI (Recursive Self-Improvement) Recursive Drift Heavy Duty Solver Discovery Model Agent Team\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-06-sv101-ai最快半年跑通自进化-验证与品味是最后门槛/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/cfe8fa9f8e3fa476-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"硅\"><span class=\"dur\">1:10:54</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">硅谷101</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0706</span></div>\n<h2>Self-evolving AI could close the loop in six months, but the model will quietly drift</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The inflection point for RSI is models becoming capable of long-horizon tasks. Apodex&#x27;s chief scientist says the self-evolution loop could close in as little as six months, but recursive drift and the model&#x27;s taste will need human gatekeeping for a long time yet.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI self-evolution</span><span class=\"tag\">RSI</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"The narcissism epidemic is media hype: the data doesn&#x27;t support it, and narcissists themselves suffer more The much-hyped ‘narcissism epidemic’ has little data behind it; narcissism as measured by the NPI has actually been falling in recent years. True NPD affects about 1%, patients often carry depression and anxiety alongside it, and treatment works but takes years. Science Vs Science Vs Narcissists: Are We Surrounded? Narcissism NPD Personality disorders Psychotherapy Workplace relationships Science communication NPI (Narcissistic Personality Inventory) NPD (Narcissistic Personality Disorder) Grandiose narcissism Gray rocking Empathy prompt Triple E\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-02-sciencevs-没有自恋流行病-自恋者只是更痛苦/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/a3282246c3202bd6-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">44:38</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Science Vs</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0702</span></div>\n<h2>The narcissism epidemic is media hype: the data doesn&#x27;t support it, and narcissists themselves suffer more</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The much-hyped ‘narcissism epidemic’ has little data behind it; narcissism as measured by the NPI has actually been falling in recent years. True NPD affects about 1%, patients often carry depression and anxiety alongside it, and treatment works but takes years.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Narcissism</span><span class=\"tag\">NPD</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Mathematicians Become Curators; the Value Is Not in the Proof AI can solve problems, explain them, and prove theorems; the mathematician&#x27;s value shifts toward judging which path is worth taking — and toward being a curator people trust. Dwarkesh Podcast Dwarkesh Grant Sanderson – AI and the future of math Mathematics AI capability limits Verifiability Curation Learning grindability theory of mind RLVR Langlands Program\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-06-30-dwarkesh-数学家未来是策展人-价值不在证明里/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/4b8f892d1d8c883d-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"D\"><span class=\"dur\">1:33:39</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Dwarkesh Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0630</span></div>\n<h2>Mathematicians Become Curators; the Value Is Not in the Proof</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI can solve problems, explain them, and prove theorems; the mathematician&#x27;s value shifts toward judging which path is worth taking — and toward being a curator people trust.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Mathematics</span><span class=\"tag\">AI capability limits</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI&#x27;s next breakthrough isn&#x27;t training — it&#x27;s letting AI learn on the job The labs are betting RLVR will generalize into general intelligence, but the real bottlenecks are sample efficiency and continual learning. OPSD and &quot;dreaming&quot; may be the keys that let AI learn from deployment rather than from pre-training alone. Dwarkesh Podcast Dwarkesh The next big breakthrough will be AIs learning on the job Continual learning RLVR Sample efficiency OPSD AI training Architectural innovation RLVR (reinforcement learning with verifiable rewards) OPSD (on-policy self-distillation) Dreaming KV cache Sample efficiency\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-06-26-dwarkesh-ai-的下一个突破-在工作中学习-而非仅靠训练/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/dd74222aed85378e-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"D\"><span class=\"dur\">19:53</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Dwarkesh Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0626</span></div>\n<h2>AI&#x27;s next breakthrough isn&#x27;t training — it&#x27;s letting AI learn on the job</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The labs are betting RLVR will generalize into general intelligence, but the real bottlenecks are sample efficiency and continual learning. OPSD and &quot;dreaming&quot; may be the keys that let AI learn from deployment rather than from pre-training alone.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Continual learning</span><span class=\"tag\">RLVR</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Disney&#x27;s moat isn&#x27;t the IP, it&#x27;s the flywheel Walt engineered Disney&#x27;s moat is not the IP itself. It is the flywheel Walt built with engineering discipline after art and commerce married inside his head: make high-quality animation, maximise its distribution, feed it into ancillary nodes, then let the whole thing compound for decades. Acquired Acquired The Walt Disney Company IP Strategy Flywheel Effect Animation Industry Long-Term Thinking Vertical Integration Disney Flywheel Multiplane camera Cel animation Pencil test Seven Powers\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-06-22-acquired-迪士尼飞轮-艺术-商业与工程的百年复利/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/372eb871b3602a8b-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">4:31:29</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Acquired</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0622</span></div>\n<h2>Disney&#x27;s moat isn&#x27;t the IP, it&#x27;s the flywheel Walt engineered</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Disney&#x27;s moat is not the IP itself. It is the flywheel Walt built with engineering discipline after art and commerce married inside his head: make high-quality animation, maximise its distribution, feed it into ancillary nodes, then let the whole thing compound for decades.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>17</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>12</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">IP Strategy</span><span class=\"tag\">Flywheel Effect</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"parent\" data-hay=\"Mothers Aren&#x27;t Sick, Society Is: How a Depression Diagnosis Moves the Problem Burnout gets misdiagnosed as depression, and the problem is attributed to the individual brain rather than the social environment. A New Zealand study found that new mothers who had someone help with the housework every day for six months almost never developed postpartum depression, yet medication is still the first-line answer. Your Parenting Mojo Your Parenting Mojo Episode Summary 10: Burnout vs Depression: The Mental Load of Mothers Depression diagnosis Maternal burnout Psychiatric drugs Medicalization Social control Postpartum depression Burnout DSM Medicalization Benzodiazepines\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-06-15-parentmojo-妈妈不是病了-是社会病了-抑郁诊断如何转移问题/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/70c340acb32275d2-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"Y\"><span class=\"dur\">18:09</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"parent\"><span class=\"src\">Your Parenting Mojo</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0615</span></div>\n<h2>Mothers Aren&#x27;t Sick, Society Is: How a Depression Diagnosis Moves the Problem</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Burnout gets misdiagnosed as depression, and the problem is attributed to the individual brain rather than the social environment. A New Zealand study found that new mothers who had someone help with the housework every day for six months almost never developed postpartum depression, yet medication is still the first-line answer.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Depression diagnosis</span><span class=\"tag\">Maternal burnout</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"Lite-version red packets aren&#x27;t growth, they&#x27;re a harvester for the algorithm and monetization Once the demographic dividend was gone, the point of red packets, Lite apps and coupon drops was never growth — it was using monetization and the recommendation algorithm to absorb the traffic. In the AI era paid acquisition is close to useless, and growth goes back to model capability and mindshare marketing. 乱翻书 乱翻书 发券、裂变、极速版，如何用红包设计增长？丨字节跳动 第8集 User growth Lite apps Red-packet virality Coupon drops Spring Festival ops AI acquisition K-factor (viral coefficient) RY1 / RY2 / RY3 (acquisition ROI, gross-margin ROI, net-profit ROI) Red-packet middle platform\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-06-12-luanfanshu-极速版的本质不是增长-是商业化和算法/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/42a856e6750ff434-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"乱\"><span class=\"dur\">2:59:48</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">乱翻书</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0612</span></div>\n<h2>Lite-version red packets aren&#x27;t growth, they&#x27;re a harvester for the algorithm and monetization</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Once the demographic dividend was gone, the point of red packets, Lite apps and coupon drops was never growth — it was using monetization and the recommendation algorithm to absorb the traffic. In the AI era paid acquisition is close to useless, and growth goes back to model capability and mindshare marketing.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">User growth</span><span class=\"tag\">Lite apps</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"parent\" data-hay=\"ADHD Medication Changes Behavior, Not Learning Barkley likens ADHD to diabetes, yet 64% of children move in and out of the diagnostic criteria repeatedly; medication buys compliance without improving learning, the long-term MTA follow-up confirms no academic advantage, and what actually works is small-group differentiated teaching. Your Parenting Mojo Your Parenting Mojo 266: If ADHD Medication Doesn’t Help Kids Learn, What Does? ADHD Child education Drug efficacy Evidence-based teaching Behavioral intervention MTA MTA study crossover design DSM misrecognition\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-06-01-parentmojo-adhd-药物改得了行为-改不了学习/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/70c340acb32275d2-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"Y\"><span class=\"dur\">30:41</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"parent\"><span class=\"src\">Your Parenting Mojo</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0601</span></div>\n<h2>ADHD Medication Changes Behavior, Not Learning</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Barkley likens ADHD to diabetes, yet 64% of children move in and out of the diagnostic criteria repeatedly; medication buys compliance without improving learning, the long-term MTA follow-up confirms no academic advantage, and what actually works is small-group differentiated teaching.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">ADHD</span><span class=\"tag\">Child education</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"14,000 cars a year, worth more than Ford: Ferrari sells exclusivity and inclusion at once Ferrari builds only about 14,000 cars a year, yet its market value exceeds Ford&#x27;s. The trick is holding a luxury brand&#x27;s exclusivity and a sports team&#x27;s inclusiveness at the same time: scarcity manufactures the myth, community sustains the loyalty. Acquired Acquired Ferrari Ferrari Luxury goods Scarcity Brand Business model Motor racing Tifosi Classiche Purosangue\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-04-13-acquired-法拉利-卖的不是车-是排他与包容的悖论/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/b28a1307f172ac6a-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">3:59:20</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Acquired</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0413</span></div>\n<h2>14,000 cars a year, worth more than Ford: Ferrari sells exclusivity and inclusion at once</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Ferrari builds only about 14,000 cars a year, yet its market value exceeds Ford&#x27;s. The trick is holding a luxury brand&#x27;s exclusivity and a sports team&#x27;s inclusiveness at the same time: scarcity manufactures the myth, community sustains the loyalty.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Ferrari</span><span class=\"tag\">Luxury goods</span>\n</div></div></a>"]